      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "Try a fresh case. The protected packet approves deployment revision fifty-eight and a fifteen-percent target. The live service changes to revision fifty-nine before execution. The approved digest still matches. Predict whether that matching digest permits the write.",
          "start": 0.4,
          "end": 16.744,
          "duration": 16.344,
          "until": 18.244
        },
        {
          "say": "It does not: the live precondition fails, so rebuild evidence and proposal and obtain the policy-required decision. Do not fall back to an unconditional write.",
          "start": 18.244,
          "end": 28.875999999999998,
          "duration": 10.632,
          "until": 29.875999999999998
        },
        {
          "say": "In a separate approved execution, the target accepts the conditional effect but the network reply is lost. Keep the operation unknown locally until a trusted receipt or supported same-key retry reconciles it. Do not invent a new logical identity to escape uncertainty. If the service has no suitable conditional mutation or repeat-safety contract, preserve that limitation instead of claiming a local ledger made the remote effect atomic.",
          "start": 29.875999999999998,
          "end": 57.596,
          "duration": 27.72,
          "until": 58.596
        },
        {
          "say": "Localize the broken boundary. A vanished card suggests nondurable pending state. An authorized decision without resumption suggests a missing durable dispatch path. A wrong-tenant effect suggests confused identities. An edited proposal under an old digest breaks intent. High approval with poor seeded-defect detection calls for a better review process. Each repair must retain the original operation evidence and re-establish the actual failed contract.",
          "start": 58.596,
          "end": 87.42,
          "duration": 28.824,
          "until": 88.42
        }
      ],
